# Orbswap frontend config — copy to `.env.local` and edit. Every value has a
# default, so `npm run dev` with NO env file works out of the box.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env*` is gitignored. Nothing here is secret (all NEXT_PUBLIC_*, shipped to the
# browser) — never put a secret key in this file.
#
# The app targets Stellar mainnet (the "Public Global" network). Set the Freighter
# extension to Mainnet to use it.

# ── Network ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Soroban RPC. Defaults to mainnet.sorobanrpc.com. Public endpoints rate-limit —
# point this at a dedicated provider before taking real traffic.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.sorobanrpc.com

# Source account for read-only `quote` simulations. Any funded mainnet account
# works; it is never asked to sign and spends nothing.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_READ_ACCOUNT=G...

# ── Contract addresses ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The deployed addresses are committed in lib/stellar/config.ts, so nothing here is
# required. Override only to point at a different deployment — the values live in
# contracts/deployments/mainnet_stable.json.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ORBSWAP_POOL=C...        # super_pool   (SuperElliptical, 4 tokens)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ORBSWAP_FACTORY=C...     # factory
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ORBSWAP_ROUTER=C...      # router
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ORBSWAP_TICK_POOL=C...   # circle_pool  (Circular + ticks, 2 tokens)

# Token addresses are NOT env-driven — the SAC addresses are fixed and compiled into
# lib/stellar/config.ts and lib/stellar/ticks.ts. Token names/icons are display
# metadata in those files.
